],"id":"euler.lemma-5.5","kind":"claim","label":"Lemma 5.5","locator":"Lemma 5.5, Section 5","source_id":"paper","statement":"**Lemma 5.5.** There is an absolute exponent $C$ such that, for every $n\\ge0$ and every field $V$ with $\\langle V\\rangle_s=0$ and $\\kappa\\cdot V=0$, $$\\begin{equation}\n \\|C[V]\\|_{[n],\\gamma}\\le C_n\\mathsf D^C\\lambda^{-1}\\|V\\|_{[n+1],\\gamma}. \\tag{5.31}\n\\end{equation}$$ If moreover $V_t+MV+\\kappa\\partial_s\\mathsf p=f$ with $\\langle f\\rangle_s=0$ and $\\langle \\mathsf p\\rangle_s=0$, then $$\\begin{equation}\n \\|(\\partial_t+M)C[V]+\\mathbf d\\mathsf p\\|_{[n],\\gamma}\n \\le C_n\\mathsf D^C\\lambda^{-1}\n             \\bigl(\\|V\\|_{[n+1],\\gamma}+\\|f\\|_{[n+1],\\gamma}\\bigr). \\tag{5.32}\n\\end{equation}$$ For the leading oscillation $V=A_1$ on $[t_0,T]$, the source in this estimate is $f=0$.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/nodes/euler.lemma-5.5","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/nodes/euler.lemma-5.5","id":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/edges/%5B%22euler.lemma-5.5%22%2C%22euler.lemma-d.1%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/edges/%5B%22euler.lemma-5.5%22%2C%22euler.lemma-d.1%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","semantic_class":"curated_argument_support","to":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/nodes/euler.lemma-d.1"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/nodes/euler.lemma-5.5","id":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/edges/%5B%22euler.lemma-5.5%22%2C%22euler.proposition-5.1%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb